{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDuring the comment-remediation epic, Gerrit briefly advertised `main` with parent `0fe2cc2e…` while Gitiles returned 404 for that object. Ref history appeared rewound and omitted merged commit `2a93f180…`. `git fetch gerrit main` returned timeout/HTTP 504, and CI run `34235734839` failed checkout when Gerrit returned HTTP 502 fetching change 2834. The service later recovered: the parent became readable and ref advertisement worked again.\n\nThis ticket now owns the `/rebar-debug` investigation requested by the operator. The confirmed, repo-remediable failure class is the Verified checkout path: the external checkout action first checked out the workflow dispatch/main ref, then treated Gerrit `refs/changes/...` fetch as mandatory. That made a transient Gerrit 502/504 fail CI before repository validation even when the exact patchset SHA was already fetchable from the GitHub mirror.\n\n## Plan\n- Reconstruct the CI failure and Gerrit recovery timeline from Gerrit change 2834 and GitHub Actions run 34235734839.\n- Compare failing and working checkout paths: failed `refs/changes/34/2834/1` fetch from Gerrit versus successful direct object-id fetch of `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` from the GitHub mirror.\n- Reuse the existing exact-SHA verification precedent from `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml`: fetch the patchset revision from the GitHub mirror first, fall back to Gerrit refspec only when the mirror SHA is unavailable, and reject any fallback whose FETCH_HEAD does not equal `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION`.\n- Replace the Verified-lane `checkout-gerrit-change-action` consumers in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` and the reusable Verified workflows (`_build-and-test.yml`, `_artifact-probe.yml`, `_eval-discipline.yml`, `_mutation.yml`, `_optionality.yml`, `_scanner-integration.yml`), passing a new non-secret `gerrit-revision` workflow_call input from `gerrit-verify.yaml` and `gerrit-scanner-verify.yml`.\n- Update workflow-structure tests that currently select patchset lanes by `checkout-gerrit-change-action`, including `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py`, and `tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py`.\n\n## Testing\n- RED: `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::<new Gerrit checkout resilience regression>` fails before the workflow fix because Verified still depends on `checkout-gerrit-change-action` / Gerrit refspec fetch for patchset checkout.\n- GREEN targeted: `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py`.\n- Final verification: `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8` with ambient GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The incident timeline is supported by exact Gerrit and CI evidence.\n- [ ] A proven repo-remediable root cause explains the checkout 502/504: Verified used a Gerrit-refspec-mandatory helper instead of the mirrored patchset SHA already available from dispatch inputs.\n- [ ] Verified-lane checkout remediation is implemented by mirror-SHA-first, Gerrit-refspec-fallback, and exact-SHA verification across direct and reusable Gerrit checkouts.\n- [ ] Verification evidence demonstrates the remediation."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788922871222928001,"uuid":"1ff6c354-e6de-4e50-bbd4-723239bedd17"}